-- title:
--   Cyclic Frobenius generator of K(μ_{q^N-1})/K over ℚ_q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl q` (a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$) which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $N$ be a natural number with $N > 0$. Write $L = K(\{\zeta \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q : \zeta^{q^N-1} = 1\})$ for the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $K$ all $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity of the algebraic closure, and assume $L$ is finite-dimensional over $K$ and normal over $K$. Then there is a $K$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $L$ such that, first, every $K$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\varphi$, i.e. $\varphi$ generates $\operatorname{Aut}_K(L)$; and second, there exists a natural number $a > 0$ such that for every $\zeta \in L$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ satisfies $\zeta^{q^N-1} = 1$ one has $\varphi(\zeta) = \zeta^{q^a}$. The exponent $a$ is only asserted to exist and to be positive; it is not pinned here to the residue degree of $K$.
--
--   This is the standard description of the Galois group of the unramified-type extension $K(\mu_{q^N-1})/K$ of a finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}_q$: it is cyclic, generated by a Frobenius element acting on the $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity by $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{q^a}$. It is used in the local analysis of level structures at $q$, for instance in the computation of norms from $K(\mu_{q^N-1})$ and in producing automorphisms with prescribed action on roots of unity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IntermediateField_exists_generator_frobenius_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_padic.lean

